      "kicker": "The studio",
      "h2": "A workshop in the lane where idols have been made for 300 years",
      "lede": "Nabakumar Pal came to Kumartuli from Krishnanagar in 1952 with one helper and a rented shed. His son Gopal built the studio's name in the club pujos of north Kolkata. Today his grandsons Sujit and Ranjit run it with twelve artisans, most of whom have been here over fifteen years.",
      "lede2": "We still use Ganga clay, rice straw and bamboo. We still paint the eyes on Mahalaya morning. What has changed is the ledger: orders now come by WhatsApp, and crates leave for Toronto and Dubai in July.",
      "gen": {
