    "process": {
      "kicker": "How it is made",
      "h2": "From bamboo and straw to chokkhu daan",
      "lede": "A 10 ft Durga takes about three months. Here is what happens in that time, in the order it happens.",
      "steps": {
        "items": [
          {
            "span": "1",
            "h3": "Kathamo <small>Bamboo frame</small>",
            "p": "A bamboo skeleton is tied with jute rope on a wooden base. The proportions of the whole idol are fixed here, so this is the senior artisan's job."
          },
          {
            "span": "2",
            "h3": "Khor bandha <small>Straw body</small>",
            "p": "Rice straw is bound tightly over the frame to give the figure its bulk. It is light, cheap and lets the clay grip."
          },
          {
            "span": "3",
            "h3": "Ek-mete <small>First clay coat</small>",
            "p": "Coarse Ganga clay mixed with rice husk goes on thick. It dries for a week or two depending on the rain."
          },
          {
            "span": "4",
            "h3": "Do-mete <small>Fine clay coat</small>",
            "p": "A smoother clay with jute fibre is applied and the surface is worked by hand. Cracks are filled; fingers, folds and faces take shape."
          },
          {
            "span": "5",
            "h3": "Mukh <small>The face</small>",
            "p": "Faces are cast from the studio's own moulds, then finished by hand. Each family of artisans has its own face; ours is known for a slightly longer eye."
          },
          {
            "span": "6",
            "h3": "Rong <small>Painting</small>",
            "p": "A white chalk base, then the skin colour, then the detail work. We use water-based paints that wash off in immersion."
          },
          {
            "span": "7",
            "h3": "Saaj <small>Dressing and ornaments</small>",
            "p": "Sari, crown, weapons and the sholar or daker saaj go on. The lion gets his mane. This is the week the lane fills with visitors."
          },
          {
            "span": "8",
            "h3": "Chokkhu daan <small>Painting the eyes</small>",
            "p": "Done last, traditionally on Mahalaya, by the head of the family. The idol is considered awake from this moment and is handled with care until delivery."
          }
        ]
      },
